  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Angle limit \"Rotation\" can be described with a curve, but it cannot cross over to the opposite sign as the curve is clamped to [0:1] range (consistent with all other curve parameters).\nThis means it's not possible to describe an angle limit that crosses over to the opposite sign (from 45 to -20 for instance).\nThe desired outcome is the ability to describe more complex mechanical systems using PhysBones where some specific joints have different liberties than others. The current way to achieve that would be by using curves to describe it.",
